  "notes": "Originally a military term meaning the complete destruction of a force, but now widely used in casual speech and gaming.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {部隊|ぶたい}が{全滅|ぜんめつ}する (a unit is annihilated)\n- {全滅|ぜんめつ}させる (wipe out completely)\n- パーティーが{全滅|ぜんめつ}する (the party gets wiped out — gaming)\n\nIn gaming and casual speech, {全滅|ぜんめつ} is often used humorously for non-lethal situations, such as all members of a group failing a test or all items selling out.",
